y and promptly — `zedagent` parsed it at 22:19:00.316 (setting `lastProcessedConfig` in-process per `parseconfig.go:211`), the volume `zvol-provisioned-test` was created by 22:19:11, and the DPC switch from the bootstrap \"lastresort\" network to the controller-assigned \"zedagent\" network completed successfully (`DPC_SUCCESS`) by 22:19:34. The problem is that this `LastProcessedConfig` value is only surfaced to the controller via a periodic `metrics` POST (`handlemetrics.go:648`), not via the device-info channel — and device logs show exactly one metrics-send attempt in the whole test window, which started around 22:18:42 (right at boot, before the DPC switch) and then hung for the full 120s client timeout, finally failing at 22:21:00.327 with `sendMetricsProtobufByURL status 0 failed: ... context deadline exceeded (Client.Timeout exceeded while awaiting headers)`, logged alongside a watchdog warning `StillRunning(zedagentmetrics) took a long time: 138`. So the one metrics report that would have carried the updated `LastProcessedConfig` got wedged on a connection/route established before the network reconfiguration and was never retried in time, even though `PublishDeviceInfo` sends succeeded repeatedly throughout (including right after the DPC switch) — the harness's 2-minute wait expired at almost exactly the same moment (22:21:00) the stuck metrics call timed out.\n\n**Ledger check:** No prior entry in `live-ledger.md` matches this signature (`TestZVolProvisionedSizeReported`, `LastProcessedConfig` timeout, or `sendMetricsProtobufByURL`/metrics-POST hang) — this appears to be a new, not-previously-recorded failure mode, not a repeat of anything documented so far.\n\n**Shared cause with this run:** No other failure has been investigated in this run yet, so there's nothing to correlate it against.\n\nNo PR diff was supplied for this investigation, so no relatedness assessment is given.","time":{"start":1794088936000,"stop":1794089337240,"duration":401240}},{"uid"